   "date": "2015-08-10T14:46:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: Retrieving the row and column information after user clicks on a heatmap",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">In the <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/reference/shiny/latest/nearPoints.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/reference/shiny/latest/nearPoints.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391799126000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JBY7HDIm71a4gVsUrs8O2\">doc for nearPoints</a> it says this under Details:<div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">It is also possible for this function to return all rows from the input data frame, but with an additional column </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&#39;Source Code Pro&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:nowrap;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\">selected_</code><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">, which indicates which rows of the input data frame are selected by the brush (</span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&#39;Source Code Pro&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:nowrap;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\">TRUE</code><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"> for selected, </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&#39;Source Code Pro&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:nowrap;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\">FALSE</code><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"> for not-selected). This is enabled by setting </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:&#39;Source Code Pro&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:nowrap;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\">allRows=TRUE</code><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"> option. If this is used, the resulting data frame will not be sorted by distance to the mouse event.</span></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Would having the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">selected_</font> column be helpful?  </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
